{
  "_README": [
    "===========================================================================",
    "  TARGET TABLE  -  THIS FILE IS NEVER SERVED TO THE BROWSER.",
    "  pingsrv.py refuses to serve *.json / *.py, and /api/games returns only",
    "  ids and labels. Hosts below stay on the server.",
    "===========================================================================",
    "",
    "  What the defaults are:",
    "  Public regional network endpoints (Vultr / Hetzner speed-test hosts and",
    "  anycast resolvers) that sit in the SAME data-center regions the listed",
    "  games run their servers in. They measure the quality of the route from",
    "  this server to that region - which is what you actually want to know -",
    "  but they are NOT the game's own servers. Every host here was verified to",
    "  resolve; no invented addresses.",
    "",
    "  To use real game endpoints instead:",
    "  replace the \"host\" values below with the ones you trust. Format:",
    "      \"host\": \"1.2.3.4\"            -> ICMP ping (best: real packet loss)",
    "      \"host\": \"name.example.com\"   -> resolved once, then ICMP",
    "      \"port\": 443                  -> optional; used only for TCP mode",
    "                                       (fallback when ICMP is blocked)",
    "  Add/remove games and regions freely. Ids must be [a-z0-9_-] and unique.",
    "",
    "  After editing:  systemctl restart gameping   (or just reload the page -",
    "  the file is re-read whenever its mtime changes)."
  ],

